%% mad_held_links_boot.glp — a forwarded link is held at both of its ends, two
%% reports, two answers, and the value is delivered (IGLP madglp-spec \S Held
%% Links; the Implementation Notes' "Held links").
%%
%% alice, the anchor, sends the writer end of a variable to bob and waits on its
%% reader; bob forwards the end to carol, who binds it.  carol's runtime holds
%% her assignment --- the end reached her from bob, not from alice --- and
%% reports pending_link(Name, bob) on her network input; her program authorises,
%% and the value goes to alice.  alice's runtime holds it --- it came from carol,
%% to whom alice exported nothing --- and reports pending_link(Name, carol); her
%% program authorises, the assignment is applied, and alice's reader delivers.
%% The agent code is the program directory mad_held_links/, which the boot
%% harness loads in every isolate with this boot clause on top.

procedure boot.
boot :-
    agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@alice,
    say(alice_init, alice, [bob], ch(_?, _))@alice,
    agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@bob,
    say(bob_init, bob, [carol], ch(_?, _))@bob,
    agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@carol,
    say(carol_init, carol, [], ch(_?, _))@carol.

%% Every agent's initial goal is agent(ch(_?,_),ch(_?,_)), the person channel first and the network channel second (GLP-Spec maglp.tex, Definition "Multiagent GLP"), which the program, mad_held_links/, answers: a boot defines no agent/2, and the person goal's first act names the entry the program starts (IGLP 30c04c5, Implementation Notes, "Boot").  The person scripted at each agent, say/4, run on its person channel in the person's place, tells the agent the entry, with its own key and the keys of the peers its person knows, its ground arguments; an agent is its public key, and a readable name here is a variable standing for one (Remark "Agent Names"), the agent's key having been made at its spawn.

%% The person at each agent: it tells the agent its role, its key and the keys of the peers it knows, its ground arguments, and reads nothing.
PersonSays ::= init(Constant, Key, List(Key)).

exported procedure say(Constant?, Key?, List(Key)?, Channel(Stream(Constant), Stream(PersonSays))?).
say(R, Me, Ps, ch(_, [init(R?, Me?, Ps?)])).
